  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical assistance to support Angola on safety and quality standards towards a national sustainable and inclusive economic growth.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The main scope of this contract is to strengthen national capacities to ensure compliance with safety and technical standards and with WTO/SPS Agreement in order to increase and diversify sustainable inclusive economic growth. The intervention addresses the following three main fields of activity: Quality Infrastructure (Metrology, Conformity Assessment, Certification and Accreditation, Standards and Testing); Sanitary and Phytosanitary Measures (WTO-SPS Agreement); Technical Barriers to Trade. The purposes of the contract are (i) to provide technical assistance, institutional capacity building, training, advocacy, awareness raising and sensitization to the relevant public and private stakeholders in the above mentioned fields and (ii) to support the upgrading of national laboratorial capacity, especially to the Ministry of Agriculture and Fisheries Food Safety Laboratory (technical assistance, training, procurement and supply of lab equipment), but also to the Ministry of Industry and Commerce - INIQ and INACOQ - and Ministry of Health laboratories (training on related issues), to ensure compliance with safety and technical standards and SPS measures.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
